- [N2] Omitted trace (input 3): i1:For TS recruitment, the first step is to advise unsuccessful candidates. -> i5:However, if the terms and conditions of the offer for a candidate need to be sorted out -> i6:if the candidate has accepted a voluntary redundancy. -> i7:if the candidate has accepted -> i9:further investigation is required. -> i10:The recruitment manager sends an Appointment Approval form -> i11:which is then received by the next level manager. -> i14:if the approver is an existing employee -> i15:If the form is approved -> i16:the recruitment manager sends the form and other documentation -> i17:which is received by the client HR. -> i18:The HR department scans the completed form and records the position against the stored position in GovSource. -> i19:If there are any variations -> i20:a complete business case is required. -> i22:The Appointment Approval is carried forward. -> i23:If the position requires a medical assessment -> i24:it is applicable for a 12% rate. -> i26:it is important to note that it can take up to 21 days to arrange and complete. -> i27:The TS HR coordinator informs the recruitment manager -> i28:who then liaises with the HR representative to confirm the offer to the candidate. -> i29:If the assessment is not satisfactory -> i30:the next candidate on the shortlist should be contacted. -> i44:Finally, the process ends.
